    "description": "Boldyn Networks provides neutral-host wireless, distributed antenna systems, private networks, Wi-Fi, and related fiber infrastructure for transit systems, venues, campuses, cities, and mobile carriers. Its customers or end markets include mobile network operators, public-sector transport authorities, venue owners, enterprises, and municipalities. The operating model is a network infrastructure model that combines long-lived physical assets with multi-tenant service contracts. Operations are concentrated in major metropolitan markets in the United States and Canada alongside international operations. Public materials indicate a business lineage that dates to 1923 and a North American footprint built through projects such as Mobilitie and Transit Wireless. Current ownership includes CPP Investments and AIMCo, which disclosed their positions in 2024, while Manulife Investment Management remains a minority investor in certain U.S. digital infrastructure assets.",
